# Intent: give back internal RAM without moving any stack to PSRAM (the unit stalled in 0.2.24 and the PSRAM stack was the prime suspect; 055 tests that separately). Measured least stack left in the 0.2.25 host log: audio_input 3,808 of 6,144 (use 2,336), audio_output 2,680 of 4,096 (use 1,416), ws_reconnect 4,432 of 6,144 (use 1,712). They shrink to 4,096, 3,072 and 4,096, which keeps at least 1.7 KB of margin over the measured peak: 5 KB back. The LVGL draw buffer was 20 display lines (12,800 bytes of DMA RAM); it is now 10 lines (6,400 bytes): 6.4 KB back, at the cost of twice as many display transfers for a full-screen redraw (the face redraws small regions). About 11 KB in all. The opus stack (24,576, least left 4,540) and the stackchan task (least left 1,428) are not touched.
# Upstream: 78/xiaozhi-esp32 main/audio/audio_service.cc, main/protocols/websocket_protocol.cc; m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc (MIT). Applies after 057 with --unidiff-zero.
# Check after a flash: "unit memory: heap_stats" int_free about 11 KB higher than before, stack_stats: audio_input, audio_output and ws_reconnect still above 1,500 bytes left; no visible tearing or slowness in the face.
